  "content": {
    "id": "p40-q6-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "6",
    "prompt": "The linear model shows how an employee is paid on commission.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [
      {
        "id": "p40-q6-graph",
        "role": "question",
        "format": "tikz",
        "code": "% mathsmap-diagram-colours {\"version\":1,\"kind\":\"graph\",\"base\":[],\"semantic\":[{\"name\":\"modelBlue\",\"hex\":\"268CFF\",\"reason\":\"linear-model graph series\"}],\"reference\":\"source page 40, p40-q6-graph\"}\n\\begin{tikzpicture}[x=0.001cm,y=0.01cm]\n\\special{dvisvgm:raw <metadata data-graph-strokes=\"1\"/>}\n\\definecolor{modelBlue}{HTML}{268CFF}\n\\draw[black,opacity=0.22,line width=0.15pt,xstep=500,ystep=50] (0,0) grid (6000,600);\n\\draw[black,opacity=0.22,line width=0.25pt,xstep=1000,ystep=100] (0,0) grid (6000,600);\n\\draw[black,->,line width=0.5pt] (0,0)--(6350,0);\n\\draw[black,->,line width=0.5pt] (0,0)--(0,630);\n\\foreach \\x in {500,1000,...,6000}{\\draw[black,line width=0.4pt] (\\x,-7)--(\\x,7);}\n\\foreach \\y in {50,100,...,600}{\\draw[black,line width=0.4pt] (-70,\\y)--(70,\\y);}\n\\foreach \\x in {1000,2000,...,6000}{\\node[below,font=\\fontsize{8.5}{10}\\selectfont,inner sep=0.2pt] at (\\x,-12) {\\special{dvisvgm:raw <g data-graph-text=\"tick\">}\\x\\special{dvisvgm:raw </g>}};}\n\\foreach \\y in {100,200,...,600}{\\node[left,font=\\fontsize{8.5}{10}\\selectfont,inner sep=0.2pt] at (-100,\\y) {\\special{dvisvgm:raw <g data-graph-text=\"tick\">}\\y\\special{dvisvgm:raw </g>}};}\n\\node[below,font=\\fontsize{10}{12}\\selectfont] at (3000,-65) {Sales (\\$)};\n\\node[rotate=90,font=\\fontsize{10}{12}\\selectfont] at (-1000,300) {Pay (\\$)};\n\\draw[modelBlue,->,line width=0.8pt] plot[domain=0:6300,samples=2] (\\x,{0.05*\\x+200});\n\\end{tikzpicture}",
        "src": null,
        "widthMm": 80,
        "alt": "Mathematical diagram",
        "overlayOf": null,
        "transparent": false,
        "axes": null,
        "spec": {
          "sourcePage": 40,
          "sourceRegion": "Question 6, lower-left graph",
          "description": "Sales–pay graph with arrowed axes, sales labels from 1000 to 6000, pay labels from 100 to 600, and grid subdivisions of 500 sales and 50 pay.",
          "mathematics": "The line begins at (0,200), passes through (2000,300) and (6000,500), and continues with an arrow. Its equation is P=0.05S+200.",
          "answerVisibility": "The supplied model line is visible in the question; no response answers or extra reading guides are added."
        },
        "derived": false,
        "reviewStatus": "needs-review"
      }
    ],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p40-q6-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "What was the value of sales if the salesperson was paid $\\$300$ for the week?",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\$2000$",
          "worked": "Read across from a pay of $\\$300$ to the line, then down to the sales axis: $\\$2000$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 12
      },
      {
        "id": "p40-q6-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "What is the salesperson’s pay if she sold $\\$5000$ worth of goods?",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\$450$",
          "worked": "Read up from sales of $\\$5000$ to the line, then across to the pay axis: $\\$450$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 12
      },
      {
        "id": "p40-q6-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "What retainer is this employee paid?",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\$200$",
          "worked": "The pay-axis intercept is $\\$200$. This is the fixed pay when sales are zero, so the retainer is $\\$200$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 12
      },
      {
        "id": "p40-q6-d",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": "What is this employee’s rate of commission?",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$5\\%$",
          "worked": "Using $(0,200)$ and $(2000,300)$ from the graph:\n$$\\begin{aligned}m&=\\frac{300-200}{2000-0}\\\\m&=0.05\\end{aligned}$$\nThe employee earns $\\$0.05$ per dollar of sales, so the commission rate is $5\\%$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 24
      },
      {
        "id": "p40-q6-e",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "e",
        "prompt": "Write an equation relating pay $P$ and sales $S$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$P=0.05S+200$",
          "worked": "The gradient is $0.05$ and the pay-axis intercept is $200$.\n$$\\begin{aligned}P&=mS+c\\\\P&=0.05S+200\\end{aligned}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 18
      },
      {
        "id": "p40-q6-root-bank-p40-q6-f",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "f",
        "prompt": "Find the pay for $\\$4000$ of sales.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\$400$",
          "worked": "Substitute $S=4000$ into the model.\n$$P=0.05(4000)+200=400$$\nThe pay is $\\$400$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 12
      },
      {
        "id": "p40-q6-root-bank-p40-q6-g",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "g",
        "prompt": "What sales are needed to earn twice the pay received for $\\$2000$ of sales?",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\$8000$ of sales gives $\\$600$ pay.",
          "worked": "Sales of $\\$2000$ give $\\$300$ pay, so twice the pay is $\\$600$.\n$$\\begin{aligned}600&=0.05S+200\\\\400&=0.05S\\\\S&=8000\\end{aligned}$$\nSales of $\\$8000$ are needed.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 24
      },
      {
        "id": "p40-q6-root-bank-p40-q6-h",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "h",
        "prompt": "Explain why doubling sales from $\\$2000$ does not double total pay.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "Only the commission doubles; the $\\$200$ retainer stays fixed.",
          "worked": "Pay rises from $\\$300$ to $\\$400$ when sales double from $\\$2000$ to $\\$4000$. The commission doubles from $\\$100$ to $\\$200$, but the $\\$200$ retainer stays fixed.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 18
      }
    ],
    "diagramPlacement": "beside-prompt"
  },
